  "id": "behavioral-avoidance-test",
  "term": "behavioral avoidance test",
  "definition": "A behavioral avoidance test is a practical assessment in which a person is asked to face a situation they have been avoiding so their avoidance and actual performance can be observed. In this source, it refers to a post-treatment driving test in real traffic used to see whether patients could carry out previously feared driving tasks.",
